{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> In my opinion the plain sense is that Aaron stretched out his hand and struck the Nile, and he stretched out his hand against all the directions in the land of Egypt, to turn every river in the land of Egypt; and the meaning of \"in all the kingdom of Egypt\":" "And the phrase \"the waters of Egypt\" is a general statement, and the specification refers to their rivers, which are not the Nile but the Shihor, and other rivers in the land of Egypt — for the blood was throughout their entire land." "<b>and upon their rivers.</b> Plural form, because the Nile is in many places." "<b>their pools.</b> Waters gathered by themselves from rainwater." "<b>and all their gathered waters.</b> These are the springs and the wells and the cisterns. And the Gaon [Saadia] said that מימי is dual — sweet waters and bitter waters like the waters of the sea; therefore it is written \"He who calls the waters of the sea\" (Amos 5:8), and behold, \"the waters of the Jordan shall be cut off\" (Joshua 3:13). And the word מים, when it is in construct state, is always dual, like מימי (1 Samuel 25:11) and מימיך (Ezekiel 12:19). Also it is plural in form, for it is impossible to say מימוֹ and מימה. And we find מי in singular: \"for the waters of impurity are not sprinkled\" (Numbers 19:13). And the meaning of \"and in the wood and in the stones\" — the waters that were in the houses, in wooden vessels, or in stone basins."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {4 "Reading ובאבנים (as in the verse); the source text reads ובאבנים consistently. The phrase מי כפול rendered as 'dual' following the Gaon's grammatical analysis."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:32.122052622Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}